  This was an attempt to compare the highest mundane and artifact weapon attack
damage.

This table is adapted from art2-343.txt.

  All weapons are blessed and used with Expert skill.  (Except 
Stormbringer.  No class can reach Expert.)


Modifications to the original table:

  - Stormbringer is at skilled.  (No class can reach Expert with it.)
  - Longbow of Diana is used by a Expert Ranger firing blessed +7 arrows,
    instead of +0.
  - All ordinary silver weapons have been added.
  - Some other ordinary weapons have been added, particularly multishot   
    missiles.  Missile weapons should have range 9, compared to range
    1 for melee weapons.  Thrown silver daggers are omitted due to rarity.
  - +2 Magicbane has been replaced with +7 Magicbane.
  - Twohanded weapons are marked with a *.

  - Artifact and silver weapon damage is in general overstated due to assumption
    of silver-hating on the part of the targets.
  - Mundane and Longbow of Diana damage is slightly overstated due to assumption
    of blessed damage.

  Notes: 

  - Stormbringer, the Staff of Aesculapius, and Fire Brand are no better 
    than ordinary weapons against demons.  Demons can't be level drained 
    and are fire resistant.

  - Demonbane against non-demons is no better than an ordinary long sword.
   
  - Silver weapons get +10.5 vs Demons, multiplied by the number of hits.

  - Vorpal blade and the Tsurugi of Murumasa have a 5% chance of instakill 
    which was not figured in.


